{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a7c4e2b1-6d8f-4c91-9e3a-2b5d8f01c4a6",
    "name": "agentic-rag-platform",
    "description": "Example requests for the local [agentic-rag-platform](https://github.com/saequus/agentic-rag-platform) API.\n\nStart the API from the repo root:\n\n    uv run fastapi dev src/agentic_rag_platform/main.py --port 8000\n\nInteractive OpenAPI docs: [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs)\n\nMachine-readable OpenAPI schema: [http://localhost:8000/openapi.json](http://localhost:8000/openapi.json)\n\nSelect the **local** environment (`baseUrl=http://localhost:8000`, `tenantId=default`). Collection variables have the same defaults and also define `corpusPath` and `samplePdfPath`.\n\nEndpoints covered: `GET /health`, `POST /chat`, `POST /ingest`, `POST /search`.\n\nNotes:\n\n- There is no request-body field to override the LLM provider. The running process uses `LLM_PROVIDER` from `.env` (`xai` by default, or `openai` / `anthropic`). Restart the API after changing it.\n- Search uses `k` (1–100), not `top_k`. Tenant scoping is `tenant_id`.\n- `POST /ingest` resolves `source_path` on the API host. The \"Ingest corpus\" request embeds every PDF under `data/raw` and can take several minutes — prefer the single-file request unless you intend a full ingest.\n- Example responses are illustrative (from unit tests and the README), not live captures.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.postman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('JSON shape: status, provider, model', function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status', 'ok');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('provider').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('model').that.is.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  ""
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liveness check. Returns the configured LLM provider and model name."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Example 200",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "health"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "Liveness check. Returns the configured LLM provider and model name."
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"provider\": \"xai\",\n  \"model\": \"grok-4.7\"\n}"
